Subject: Default -disable-usage-reports to true in the package build

Origin: DHI-internal (packaging default for the anonymous usage report opt-out)
Description: Make the agent send no anonymous usage reports unless -disable-usage-reports=false is passed.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/grafana/synthetic-monitoring-agent 82d4755820c4b44e141ccba6b69add655ea8a7c6
Verify: test tests/usage_test.go::TestUsageReportsOffByDefault
Forwarded: not-needed (packaging default; upstream keeps reports on by default)
Drop-When: never: packaging default for this product; drop only if the package stops shipping the upstream agent

The upstream agent posts usage reports to stats.grafana.org unless the runtime flag is set, and the flag has no environment variable or build switch. Changing the flag default in the packaged source makes the agent opt out without an extra argument, since the image entrypoint replaces any command-line defaults.

diff --git a/cmd/synthetic-monitoring-agent/main.go b/cmd/synthetic-monitoring-agent/main.go
index 0aa3a233..b465eb33 100644
--- a/cmd/synthetic-monitoring-agent/main.go
+++ b/cmd/synthetic-monitoring-agent/main.go
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ func run(args []string, stdout io.Writer) error {
 	flags.IntVar(&config.TelemetryTimeSpan, "telemetry-time-span", config.TelemetryTimeSpan, "time span between telemetry push executions per tenant")
 	flags.BoolVar(&config.AutoMemLimit, "enable-auto-memlimit", config.AutoMemLimit, "automatically set GOMEMLIMIT")
 	flags.BoolVar(&config.DisableK6, "disable-k6", config.DisableK6, "disables running k6 checks on this probe")
-	flags.BoolVar(&config.DisableUsageReports, "disable-usage-reports", config.DisableUsageReports, "Disable anonymous usage reports")
+	flags.BoolVar(&config.DisableUsageReports, "disable-usage-reports", true, "Disable anonymous usage reports")
 	flags.Float64Var(&config.MemLimitRatio, "memlimit-ratio", config.MemLimitRatio, "fraction of available memory to use")
 	flags.Var(&features, "features", "optional feature flags")
 	flags.Var(&config.CacheType, "cache-type", "cache type: auto (memcached if servers provided, else local), memcached, local, or noop")
